    "## 3 — Interactive Correction Protocol (Single-Voxel Simulation)\n",
    "\n",
    "### Pre-Correction Spatial Diagnostics\n",
    "Before simulating interactive clicks, a spatial validation was conducted on baseline outliers (`train_0011` and `train_0013`) to rule out grid or affine orientation mismatches between predictions and ground-truth references.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Interactive Click Generation Strategy\n",
    "* **Single-Voxel Encoding (`sigma=0`):** Corrections simulate targeted single-voxel clicks rather than spatial Gaussian spheres or $3 \\times 3 \\times 3$ blocks.\n",
    "* **Euclidean Distance Transform (EDT):** `click_voxel_inside` computes the 3D distance transform (`distance_transform_edt`) on each error component, placing the click at the center of the maximal inscribed sphere (pole of inaccessibility) to prevent boundary placement on non-convex lesions.\n",
    "* **Iterative Budget:** 2 clicks per round (1 Foreground on the largest false-negative component, 1 Background on the largest false-positive component), accumulated across 5 inference iterations.\n",
    "* **Component Extraction:** Error components are extracted from the voxel-level difference (`pred & ~gt` for FP; `~pred & gt` for FN) using 26-connectivity."
   ]
