    "**Implementation Note — Post-Processing Scope:**\n",
    "In this pipeline, classical post-processing focuses on 3D binary hole filling (`binary_fill_holes`) and connected-component volume thresholding ($< 1.0\\text{ mL}$). Scribble-consistency enforcement (suppressing predicted components intersecting background clicks) was omitted from post-processing because temporary iterative scribble volumes were cleared during Step 3 to stay within the 20 GB workspace storage quota. All morphological operations are evaluated model-agnostically on top of the frozen baseline predictions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4 — Morphological Post-Processing & Error Decomposition\n",
    "\n",
    "To evaluate whether simple morphological heuristics improve segmentation without additional model inference, two operations were assessed on all iteration outputs:\n",
    "1. **3D Binary Hole Filling (`binary_fill_holes`):** Targets necrotic lesion cores and non-convex internal false negatives.\n",
    "2. **Component Filtering (`< 1.0 mL`):** Removes isolated high-SUV hyper-intensities (e.g., small focal artifacts, physiological uptake in kidney/bladder margins).\n",
    "\n",
    "*Evaluation distinction:* Voxel-level false positives/negatives measure total error volume, while lesion-level metrics (FPV/FNV) track connected components with zero ground-truth overlap."
   ]
