    "# Experimental Results & Final Analysis (Step 5)\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Baseline Performance (Iteration 0 — Unassisted Pretrained Network)\n",
    "On the 10-patient evaluation cohort (`train_0011` to `train_0020`, PSMA PET/CT from the DeepPSMA dataset), the unassisted `Dataset998_AutoPETV` 3D full-resolution nnU-Net baseline achieved a **Mean Dice of `0.4977`** (**Median Dice `0.5912`**), with a mean lesion-level False Positive Volume (FPV) of **`49.08 mL`** and a mean lesion-level False Negative Volume (FNV) of **`27.69 mL`** (Step 2 unfiltered baseline).\n",
    "\n",
    "The model performed strongly on high-contrast tumor burden cases such as `train_0014` ($\\text{Dice} = 0.8196$, lesion-level $\\text{FNV} = 0.00\\text{ mL}$), but completely failed on `train_0011` ($\\text{Dice} = 0.0000$, lesion-level $\\text{FNV} = 112.22\\text{ mL}$) and `train_0013` ($\\text{Dice} = 0.0175$, lesion-level $\\text{FNV} = 91.98\\text{ mL}$). Diagnostic grid and affine verification (Step 3, Cell 1) confirmed that both failures occurred on perfectly aligned volumes with large world-coordinate centroid distances ($476.8\\text{ mm}$ and $406.1\\text{ mm}$), demonstrating genuine baseline misses where human-in-the-loop interactivity is essential.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2. Interactive Segmentation Evolution (Step 3 — Single-Voxel Protocol)\n",
    "Across 5 correction rounds (2 single-voxel `sigma=0` clicks per round: 1 foreground + 1 background, accumulated across iterations), the cohort **Mean Dice increased monotonically from `0.4977` (Iteration 0) to `0.5985` (Iteration 5)**, while **Median Dice also improved steadily from `0.5912` to `0.6046`**. Both the **Mean-curve AUC** and **Mean per-patient AUC** over iterations 0–5 reached **`0.5704`**.\n",
