    "  * `train_0015`: Dice improved substantially from `0.5129` (Iter 0) to `0.7419` Pre / `0.7457` Hole (Iter 5), reducing voxel-level FN volume (Pre) from `707.75 mL` to `437.22 mL`.\n",
    "* **Qualitative Failures (False-Positive Expansion Under Forced Clicks):** While the cohort mean rose by `+0.1008` Dice and median rose to `0.6046`, the automated protocol forces 1 FG and 1 BG click at every iteration based on voxel-level differences (`~pred & gt`). On cases with moderate baseline performance such as `train_0018` (Dice: `0.6031` $\\to$ `0.4982` at Iter 1 $\\to$ `0.5112` at Iter 5) and `train_0019` (Dice: `0.5730` $\\to$ `0.5512` at Iter 5), placing additional foreground clicks on the unsegmented rim/boundary of subtle uptake caused the network to over-segment nearby physiological uptake, increasing `train_0018`'s voxel-level FP volume (Full) from `94.66 mL` (Iter 0) to `184.45 mL` (Iter 5).\n",
